---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import '../../styles/study.css';
import { goodrichMarkup } from '../../study/generated-slices13.js';

const title = 'Chapter 4 Exercise 6 — Recursive harmonic numbers — Sam Lair';
const description = 'A static, bounded rendering of a selected recursive harmonic-number source slice.';
---

<Site title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="article study-article glass">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/study/katex.css" />
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Sam Lair home</a>
    <div class="article-meta"><span>Study</span><span>Algorithms</span></div>
    <h1>Chapter 4 Exercise 6 — Recursive harmonic numbers</h1>
    <p class="article-lead">The recursive definition, its implementation, and a bounded input contract.</p>
    <section class="study-notice" aria-labelledby="goodrich-example-title">
      <h2 id="goodrich-example-title">Read-only example</h2>
      <p>Browser execution is not enabled yet; this page presents the algorithm and its finite floating-point behavior for study.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="study-mdx" aria-label="Compiled Goodrich study page" set:html={goodrichMarkup}></section>
    <section class="study-provenance" aria-labelledby="goodrich-provenance-title">
      <h2 id="goodrich-provenance-title">Source and attribution</h2>
      <p>The selected source is attributed to Samuel Lair under GPL-3.0. The exact revision, blob, copied bytes, and input guard are recorded in the provenance manifest.</p>
      <p><a href="/study/provenance/goodrich-ch4-ex6-harmonic.json">Read the Goodrich provenance manifest</a></p>
      <p><a href="/study/licenses/lehman-GPL-3.0.txt">GPL-3.0 source license</a> · <a href="/study/licenses/katex-LICENSE.txt">KaTeX license</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Site>
